  "gotchas": [
    {
      "severity": "info",
      "text": "Image: the recipe boot script defaults to spark-vllm:qwen38, which its run log describes as eugr/spark-vllm:latest of 2026-08-14 with ffmpeg 6.1.1 added, and which is not published. These rows ran on eugr/spark-vllm:nightly-20260814, repo digest sha256:ab89584706575a7af48a3d5a2a92bc48a5432781fb87925a181d8bb5eab4f5d3, image id a0cb301789ef, the id the recipe run log records for eugr/spark-vllm:latest. Its build-metadata.yaml names vllm-project/vllm main aa3100357 with no extra pull requests. ffmpeg is absent; it matters only for video and image input."
    },
    {
      "severity": "info",
      "text": "Boot lottery: this boot allocated 72.47 GiB of KV cache, 1,250,962 tokens, 4.77x concurrency at 262144, with gpu-memory-utilization 0.85 and 114.83 of 121.63 GiB free at startup. The recipe README reports 1,161,326 tokens (4.43x) for the same settings on its machine. vLLM padded the KV groups with 2 and 4 layers and warns the second may waste up to 25 per cent of that group."
    },
    {
      "severity": "info",
      "text": "KV cache dtype is not set by the recipe (kv-cache-dtype auto), but unsloth/Qwen3.8-27B-NVFP4 carries a static per-tensor 8-bit float kv_cache_scheme in its quantization_config, and FlashInfer resolved kv_cache_dtype float8_e4m3fn with the xqa decode backend. The recipe omits --attention-backend on purpose; vLLM picked FLASHINFER out of FLASHINFER and TRITON_ATTN, and FlashInfer serves the draft model non-causal attention."
    },
    {
      "severity": "info",
      "text": "Neither the target nor the drafter is pinned. unsloth/Qwen3.8-27B-NVFP4 resolved to main f0b7c9e7 (2026-09-08). The recipe run log names snapshot a767244, which no longer exists in the repository history after the 2026-08-15 super-squash; every file except README.md has the same content hash at 16b6615a (the squash), 57926bac and f0b7c9e7. Doopeworld/Qwen3.8-27B-DSpark-vLLM resolved to ebaa0919 (2026-08-16), its only upload: 5 layers, bf16, block_size 7, 2.6 GB."
    },
    {
      "severity": "info",
      "text": "DSpark runs with 14 speculative tokens against a drafter whose config says block_size 7, and probabilistic draft sampling. During the pre-run sanity requests (thinking on and off, greedy, 64 + 512 + 512 tokens) vLLM counted 339 drafts, 4,746 draft tokens and 757 accepted, 16 per cent, a mean acceptance length of 3.2 tokens per step; positions 9 to 14 accepted almost nothing on prose-like output. The README 75 to 78 tok/s is a 3,000-token edit that copies code already in the prompt, where it reports 68 per cent acceptance."
    },
    {
      "severity": "info",
      "text": "vLLM reads generation_config.json from the target and overrides its own sampling defaults with temperature 1.0, top_k 20, top_p 0.95. Every request here sets temperature 0 and seed 42."
    },
    {
      "severity": "info",
      "text": "Speed rows force thinking off per request with chat_template_kwargs enable_thinking false. Eval rows use the served default, which is thinking on at full length, because the chat template comes from the target repository unmodified; the recipe sets no reasoning level of its own."
    },
    {
      "severity": "info",
      "text": "The server runs without an API key and uses host networking on port 8888, the script default. The script also passes VLLM_USE_FLASHINFER_MOE_FP4=0, which this vLLM build logs as an unknown environment variable, and VLLM_MARLIN_USE_ATOMIC_ADD=1."
    },
    {
      "severity": "info",
      "text": "Boot took 11 minutes from docker run to the first answered request: 160 s to load the 22 GB target from a cold page cache, about 2.5 minutes of FlashInfer fp4_gemm autotuning, 50 s of torch.compile and 99 s of CUDA graph capture (51 piecewise and 33 full sizes up to 512 tokens, plus 34 DSpark sizes)."
    }
